{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_zymbymxa4hrr3uj4oyrbmdfgukh5sdfjwx5fpgyj7k7mrnwszcdq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. **39 configurations × 40 differential tests, 0 failures, empty symbol diff everywhere.**\n\n## Bug found and fixed\n\nOne real divergence: **`mdcore.c`/`mdmain.c` print with C `printf`, which is block-buffered when stdout is a pipe.** The Rust used `std::io::stdout()` with an explicit flush per call, so the library's output interleaved differently with a consumer's own output. Caught by the subprocess test (`examples/socall`):\n\n```\nC:    \"ret=10\\nhelper.call=0 helper.acc=10\\n\"\nRust: \"helper.call=0 helper.acc=10\\nret=10\\n\"\n```\n\nFixed by calling libc `printf` with the identical format strings in `src/mdcore.rs` and `src/main.rs`. The `argc < 3` usage message now also writes `argv[0]` as **raw bytes** (C's `%s`) rather than `from_utf8_lossy`.\n\n## Artifacts (crate root)\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — 8 C symbols (`op_add/sub/mul`, `helper_call/ptr`, `use_generated`, `G_OP`, `G_OP_NAME`), all exported by Rust; lists byte-identical. Documents that `accum_<OP>` is `static` in C so must be exported by neither.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 21 rows. Notable C quirk replicated verbatim: `DISPATCH_REP`'s `switch` has **cases 0–6 only**, so `use_generated(7)` returns `INIT` even though `REP7` exists and `RUN_LOOP` uses it at `REPEAT=7`.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 54 rows across the 24 `OP`×`REPEAT` builds, all 9 entry points (incl. both data symbols), `atoi` shapes, and the 15 Cargo-only feature combos.\n\n## Harness sensitivity (fault injection)\n\nSix mutations injected, all caught, all reverted (sources verified byte-identical after):\n\n| mutation | tests failed |\n|---|---|\n| `op_add` → `a+b+1` | 22 |\n| `dispatch_rep` accepts `n==7` | 4 |\n| `INIT_mul` 1→2 | 22 |\n| `run_loop` `REPEAT-1` | 14 |\n| `atoi` overflow → 0 | 2 |\n| `G_OP_NAME` `\"sub\"`→`\"SUB\"` | 11 |\n\n## Two things worth knowing\n\n1. **`cargo test` does not rebuild the `cdylib`** — only the lib test harness. A bare `cargo test` after switching features silently loads a stale `.so`. Added a self-check that fails with an actionable message; use `./run_diff.sh`, which does `cargo build` first.\n2. `cargo check --all-targets` passes for all 140 feature combinations tried (36 single-axis + 104 multi-feature), including the empty set.\n\nNew files: `build_c.sh`, `run_diff.sh`, `run_odd_combos.sh`, `translation/tests/differential.rs`, `translation/examples/socall.rs`. `c_src/` untouched apart from the `build/` dir created by the task's documented cmake command."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2473,"cache_read_input_tokens":149154,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2473,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5700871b-c444-47b3-9f53-f2ee6d06ed4e","uuid":"9e1a340e-c97c-474d-80a3-642a7894d09e","timestamp":"2026-09-06T15:15:10.344Z"}
